From d2353484a6992032be88ba2ac20d95593815b96c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Selmo <felipe.selmo@ethereum.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:56:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Ethereum.Test.Base: attach a fixture's block access list
 to the block under test

The EIP-7928 list travels beside the block RLP; the blockchain test lane
decoded only the RLP, so Block.BlockAccessList was null on every test block
and BlockAccessListManager.PrepareForProcessing -- which requires a non-null
list -- never enabled parallel execution, whatever --parallelExecution said.

Parse the fixture's blockAccessList into a ReadOnlyBlockAccessList, round-trip
it through RLP so the block carries the encoded bytes and wire hash the way the
network path delivers them, and attach it before the block is enrolled.

Verified at 7a63aa02da on a 40-fixture generated shard, counting the
PrepareForProcessing decision per real block: --parallelExecution true gives
parallel=True with the list attached on 40 of 40; false gives parallel=False on
40 of 40; verdicts 40/40 both ways. A fixture with a corrupted delivered list
is rejected in both modes (InvalidBlockLevelAccessListHash).
